Alternatively, could we remove the need for an extension trait by putting this on the Query impl?

```rust
impl<BLAH> Query<BLAH> {
  fn iter_with<ENTITY_ITER>(&self, i: ENTITY_ITER) -> QueryIter<BLAH> {
  }
}


fn system(has_a: Query<Entity, With<A>>, bs: Query<&B>) {
   for b in bs.iter_with(&has_a) {
   }
}
```

Functionally, this is very similar to the `many` api variants. The only difference is whether or not we use const-length-arrays vs iterators. We should definitely support both as they have different uses, but we might want to unify terminology. Maybe `many_iter`, `many_for_each`, and `many_for_each_mut`?

